```
pub struct Span<'a> {
    pub style: Style,
    pub content: Cow<'a, str>,
}
```

Expand description

Represents a part of a line that is contiguous and where all characters share the same style.

A `Span` is the smallest unit of text that can be styled. It is usually combined in the [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line") type to represent a line of text where each `Span` may have a different style.

## [§](#constructor-methods)Constructor Methods

-   [`Span::default`](../prelude/struct.Span.html#method.default "associated function ratatui::prelude::Span::default") creates an span with empty content and the default style.
-   [`Span::raw`](../prelude/struct.Span.html#method.raw "associated function ratatui::prelude::Span::raw") creates an span with the specified content and the default style.
-   [`Span::styled`](../prelude/struct.Span.html#method.styled "associated function ratatui::prelude::Span::styled") creates an span with the specified content and style.

