#### pub fn [styled\_graphemes](#method.styled_graphemes)<S>( &'a self, base\_style: S, ) -> impl [Iterator](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/iterator/trait.Iterator.html "trait core::iter::traits::iterator::Iterator")<Item = [StyledGrapheme](struct.StyledGrapheme.html "struct ratatui::text::StyledGrapheme")<'a>>

where S: [Into](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")<[Style](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style")\>,

Returns an iterator over the graphemes held by this span.

`base_style` is the [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style") that will be patched with the `Span`’s `style` to get the resulting [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style").

`base_style` accepts any type that is convertible to [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style") (e.g. [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style"), [`Color`](../prelude/enum.Color.html "enum ratatui::prelude::Color"), or your own type that implements [`Into<Style>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")).

##### [§](#example-2)Example

```
use std::iter::Iterator;

use ratatui_core::style::{Style, Stylize};
use ratatui_core::text::{Span, StyledGrapheme};

let span = Span::styled("Test", Style::new().green().italic());
let style = Style::new().red().on_yellow();
assert_eq!(
    span.styled_graphemes(style)
        .collect::<Vec<StyledGrapheme>>(),
    vec![
        StyledGrapheme::new("T", Style::new().green().on_yellow().italic()),
        StyledGrapheme::new("e", Style::new().green().on_yellow().italic()),
        StyledGrapheme::new("s", Style::new().green().on_yellow().italic()),
        StyledGrapheme::new("t", Style::new().green().on_yellow().italic()),
    ],
);
```

